  "description": "The Stroma is a versatile, year-round road bike suited to the ever changing weather and road surfaces of the UK. It’s an all-road, fast gravel, endurance bike. However you want to classify it, the Stroma is an extremely capable machine – designed to be fast, responsive and supremely comfortable over distance, no matter how rough it gets.\n\nThe Stroma truly lives up to its namesake; a remote island off the rough north east coast of Scotland, battered by ferocious weather and near impenetrable tides.\n\nThe frame is constructed out of Reynolds 725 steel; a heat treated tubing famed for its strength and weight saving properties and an ideal material for the challenges posed by year round road cycling. We’ve matched this with the Brother full carbon road fork up front giving you a lightweight and responsive front end with optimum power transfer – this has also been updated for 2025 to now include internal dynamo routing – further enhancing the Stroma’s endurance credentials. The frame and fork have fitted eyelets for full mudguards and clearance for up to 38mm tyres or 32mm with mudguards.\n\nOther features include thru-axle flat-mount dropouts, replaceable dropout inserts, 2 x bottle cage and rear rack mounts, and Di2 routing – which neatly doubles up as internal routing for a rear dynamo light.",
